      "claim": "Paritaprevir, a peptidomimetic protease inhibitor, had absolute oral bioavailability of 52.6% from a tablet and approximately 50% after oral administration, further supporting high F for this compound class.",
      "card_ids": ["C03", "C24", "C54"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The poor-bioavailability contexts (danavorexton, argatroban, rifampin-induced propafenone) are structurally or conditionally distant from the query and do not provide affirmative threshold-relevant evidence for F<20%.",
